1
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:17,977
The End of the Sea Did you know there's an

2
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:20,257
awesome treasure hidden
at the end of the sea?

3
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:22,977
And anyone who finds it,
the King of the Pirates!

4
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:24,517
Is that exciting or what?

5
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:28,247
There are incredible adventures
out there just waiting for us!

6
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:31,760
Bon voyage.

7
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:35,397
Have the courage that sail and believe!

8
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:37,280
And we will see.

9
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:40,697
A glimpse of the sun rising?

10
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:43,360
On our tomorrow.

11
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:47,877
Back when we first started.

12
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:50,677
We had separate horizons.

13
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:53,137
Sailed toward different dreams.

14
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,457
Things have changed now!

15
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:57,357
For together we found.

16
00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:00,057
We look through the spyglass and see.

17
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:05,597
And we know that our hearts
have brought us here.

18
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:09,237
Where the conscious points our destiny.

19
00:01:09,320 --> 00:01:13,180
There's no looking back,
take the hell with me!

20
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:17,337
Bon voyage, we can't
stop all our troubles.

21
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:19,640
Forget the past.

22
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:24,297
Though the future's
unclear, we still can smile.

23
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:26,957
We know we'll get there!

24
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:28,660
No regrets.

25
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:32,397
Every tear that we've cried only helps.

26
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:33,800
Our dreams come true.

27
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:39,660
You and those dreams
are precious in my life.

28
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:46,540
A glimpse of the sun
rising on our tomorrow?

29
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:54,840
Uh, do you mind if I call you, Issie?

30
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:59,700
Can you really tell which way the
gravity blue rider's ship is heading?

31
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:02,620
Yeah, that's amazing.

32
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:07,924
Even from this far away, you can hear the
sound of their voices inside the forest.

33
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:10,397
But are you sure you're feeling all right?

34
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:13,421
You've been trembling ever
since we picked you up.

35
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:19,480
It's just, it's just that I've
never ever been this afraid before.

36
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:25,140
Everyone's voices, everyone's
voices keep disappearing one by one.

37
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:31,740
Yes, I'm sorry, we've got to hurry, Conis.

38
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,300
Yes, father.

39
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,877
I'm finally a pirate.

40
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:42,677
I think instead of looking for the
others, I'll just look for the gold.

41
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:44,860
That was your shock, everybody.

42
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:52,147
That place over there seems like
a good spot for gold to hide.

43
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:53,740
Who knows?

44
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:56,853
Maybe the others will end up there, too.

45
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:13,380
Hold on!

46
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:15,457
Where do you think you're going?

47
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:17,797
I'm sorry, but I've got to locate Enero.

48
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,077
You can't leave a lady.

49
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,572
I'm a lone way out here.

50
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:22,360
I already said I was sorry.

51
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,437
I don't have time to
explain my suspicions,

52
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:28,960
but I fear that my men's
lives may be in great danger.

53
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:32,020
No, this whole land may be in danger.

54
00:03:33,260 --> 00:03:35,340
Pierre, can you fly? Pierre!

55
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:37,040
That's all?

56
00:03:38,240 --> 00:03:41,380
Hold it right there, you heartless brute!

57
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,780
How could you?

58
00:03:43,020 --> 00:03:44,477
And you call yourself a god!

59
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,390
Get back here!

60
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:46,700
Think this over!

61
00:03:56,600 --> 00:04:00,237
I guess the main thing now would be
to give these guys some first aid.

62
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:02,496
You guys are still alive, aren't you?

63
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,300
Oh, Chopper, hurry up and get back here!

64
00:04:06,620 --> 00:04:07,920
Ah! What? What?

65
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:15,670
Hazel!

66
00:04:17,920 --> 00:04:18,750
Thomas?

67
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:22,690
Hazel!

68
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:23,760
And her dad?

69
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:26,220
Dad, what are you doing here?

70
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:32,341
And would you knock it off
with that horn already?

71
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:35,860
Let me go!

72
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:39,100
Wait, no, you mustn't go. Let go!

73
00:04:39,420 --> 00:04:41,126
You can't go into the forest.

74
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:42,090
You'll be killed.

75
00:04:42,173 --> 00:04:44,747
I promise we'll only
stay for a little while.

76
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,420
I said let go!

77
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:49,017
Oh, this young lady is Issie.

78
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:51,857
Stand back, you blue sea
devil, or I'll smash you!

79
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:54,000
I'm a brave warrior of Shandora!

80
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:55,110
That's nice, kid.

81
00:04:55,193 --> 00:04:56,117
You want to fight me?

82
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,457
Have a face full of impact.

83
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:58,477
This is terrible.

84
00:04:58,560 --> 00:04:59,617
They've been burnt black.

85
00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:00,977
They need first aid at once.

86
00:05:01,060 --> 00:05:02,413
At any rate, I'm sorry.

87
00:05:02,840 --> 00:05:06,075
Now, quick, turn your ship
up the path we just came on.

88
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:09,200
We used a milky dial
to create a new river.

89
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:12,437
If you follow it, you can exit
directly to the White White Sea.

90
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,737
Quick, before the enemy
realizes we're here.

91
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:17,537
Then shouldn't you have been
a little quieter getting here?

92
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:21,460
Oh, by the way, I almost forgot
I brought something to give you.

93
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:25,490
Thank you.

94
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:07,830
What?

95
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:10,060
Or were you still here?

96
00:06:21,220 --> 00:06:22,317
I'm sorry.

97
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:24,977
I guess I must have dozed off.

98
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,720
Is something wrong?

99
00:06:27,300 --> 00:06:28,980
You seem to be in pain

100
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:32,080
I've kept my promise, haven't I?

101
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:33,971
I haven't moved a muscle.

102
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,020
I can't.

103
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,340
Beat you, can I?

104
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:49,860
No, you can't.

105
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,560
Do you understand now?

106
00:06:52,840 --> 00:06:54,540
I am living lightning.

107
00:06:56,440 --> 00:07:01,040
Try as you might, no mere man
can defeat such divine power.

108
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:06,237
Surely as a native of the sky you've seen
it flashing in the distance, haven't you?

109
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,757
Since ancient times,

110
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:11,977
men have trembled before the unknown forces
of nature and worshipped them as God.

111
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:16,178
Anything the fools could not understand
reduced them to abject terror.

112
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:20,877
No matter what happens to mankind,
whether for good or for evil,

113
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:22,901
it is said to be the work of God.

114
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:26,940
It's inevitable.

115
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:31,844
Mankind accepts that it can never
defeat the disasters of nature.

116
00:07:32,880 --> 00:07:34,000
I'm one of them.

117
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:37,680
Ahhhh!

118
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:44,120
Oh, a breath dialing.

119
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,700
Bird blade!

120
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:15,100
I have to tell Wiper, we
can't win this battle.

121
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:19,000
This is suicide.

122
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:22,658
Even if he sacrifices himself,
the reject won't work.

123
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,800
It's too late to run now.

124
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:28,797
We've got to fall back and regroup.

125
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:29,737
Or else...

126
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:30,820
or else...

127
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:40,334
Did you think that you could
move faster than lightning?

128
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:45,260
Your five minutes are up.

129
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:49,560
And now it's my turn.

130
00:08:56,760 --> 00:09:00,097
One million volt body.

131
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:02,680
WIPER!

132
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:32,800
Did you hear that?

133
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:42,520
What? What's happening?

134
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:44,840
What's wrong?

135
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,430
Aisa?

136
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:48,020
The voices!

137
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,800
They're disappearing!

138
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:02,100
Damn, I guess my electricity
traveled down the Milky Road.

139
00:10:02,700 --> 00:10:05,940
Another 20 voices vanished
after that lightning bolt.

140
00:10:06,660 --> 00:10:08,160
The stupid fools.

141
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:17,880
On the upper yard, 81 people
began the survival game.

142
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:24,580
Two hours have passed, and of that
eighty-one, fifty-six have fallen.

143
00:10:27,620 --> 00:10:30,500
Thirteen of my divine squad still remain.

144
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:36,140
Five members of the Straw
Hat crew are still with us.

145
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:39,840
And seven warriors of Shandora.

146
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:44,031
That means there are twenty-five
players still in the game.

147
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:47,649
That's a lot more survivors
than I predicted there would be.

148
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:49,100
No matter.

149
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:52,814
They'll all fall in their
turn, one right after another.

150
00:10:53,400 --> 00:10:57,640
The only real question remaining
is, who will come with me?

151
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:03,160
It's amazing!

152
00:11:03,760 --> 00:11:05,360
You're incredible, Nami!

153
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:10,180
She's all yours now and as good as new!

154
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:11,960
Yeah, thanks!

155
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:15,257
I don't know what you did, but I love it!

156
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:17,340
This thing is so fast, it's crazy!

157
00:11:17,740 --> 00:11:18,570
It's true.

158
00:11:18,653 --> 00:11:21,442
And jet dials went extinct
hundreds of years ago.

159
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,325
It's really quite astonishing.

160
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:27,345
Imagine how shocked I was to find
one aboard the Waver you left.

161
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:31,077
I fear we're running out of
things to occupy ourselves with.

162
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:34,017
We had planned to lead all
of you to the end of Skypiea,

163
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:36,688
but it seems our
circumstances have changed.

164
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,757
I guess the best thing
to do is get the ship

165
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,837
to the coast where we all agreed to meet.

166
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,477
There's really no reason to worry.

167
00:11:43,560 --> 00:11:44,854
I'm sure they're fine.

168
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:47,857
You know, when the four of
those goofballs get together,

169
00:11:47,940 --> 00:11:49,397
there's practically no stopping them.

170
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,421
There aren't any four-man groups.

171
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,224
At the most, there's maybe two.

172
00:11:55,620 --> 00:12:00,149
If there were a four-man group on the
island, I'd know about it, and I don't.

173
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:01,400
It's Mantara.

174
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:05,598
That's the power that Eneru
and his priests use, huh?

175
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:08,620
I was born able to use it.

176
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:09,670
That's why...

177
00:12:09,753 --> 00:12:11,640
that's why I'm so afraid.

178
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:16,120
You have no idea how scary it
is to hear voices disappear.

179
00:12:17,020 --> 00:12:18,961
You're not crying again, are you?

180
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:22,640
No, I'm not crying, you
stupid blue sea person!

181
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:24,628
Her waiver had broken down.

182
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:26,917
Luckily, our boat happened to pass by.

183
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:30,637
If we hadn't gotten to her when we did,
she would have been eaten by a sky shark.

184
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:33,597
What were you thinking
coming out here by yourself?

185
00:12:33,680 --> 00:12:37,386
I don't know, but I couldn't keep
sitting around doing nothing.

186
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:42,900
Lucky, and everybody.

187
00:12:47,760 --> 00:12:50,220
I hope everyone is all right.

188
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,480
Ugh, what a day.

189
00:13:08,720 --> 00:13:09,720
This is crappy.

190
00:13:10,140 --> 00:13:13,434
I'm starving and I left my
bag outside this stupid cave.

191
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:16,077
And all the fruit trees
around here are rotten.

192
00:13:16,160 --> 00:13:20,160
And all I can think about is eating
that yummy breakfast Sanji made.

193
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:23,679
What kind of messed up cave
did I wind up in anyway?

194
00:13:23,800 --> 00:13:25,918
Can't seem to find an exit anywhere.

195
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:30,457
I wonder if everybody's already
made it to this city of gold.

196
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:33,557
I bet it's all pretty and
shiny and golden and stuff.

197
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:36,117
And they probably make all
kinds of good food there too.

198
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:38,640
I can't wait to get there and find out.

199
00:13:50,620 --> 00:13:52,973
I guess I could've been walking forever.

200
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,741
I think I'll have that lunch now.

201
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,430
Who's there?

202
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:09,097
Sorry, fellow, but I don't speak bird.

203
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:13,280
If it's my food you're after,
hey, you're not getting it.

204
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:15,640
Stop staring at me.

205
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:27,747
Would you stop following me?

206
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:31,657
Listen, feather brain,
I just ate all my food.

207
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:33,217
I don't have any more, okay?

208
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:35,357
Besides, I wouldn't give
you any even if I had some,

209
00:14:35,440 --> 00:14:37,558
so get lost before I lose my temper.

210
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,217
What is your problem anyhow?

211
00:14:40,300 --> 00:14:44,117
Walking all weird with your big fat
melon head face in the wrong direction.

212
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,757
I don't want to have to
fight you, bird, but I will.

213
00:14:46,840 --> 00:14:47,670
Got it?

214
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:56,020
In three hours, a mere five of the 81
people on this island will be left standing.

215
00:14:57,820 --> 00:15:00,837
There's only one hour
left until my proclaimed

216
00:15:00,920 --> 00:15:05,340
time is up And 25
survivors currently remain.

217
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:08,560
This can't be.

218
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:10,840
What's Inaru doing here?

219
00:15:11,760 --> 00:15:13,480
He's going down.

220
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:27,840
And now, 24.

221
00:15:36,260 --> 00:15:40,080
Well, it seems all your
talk doesn't amount to much.

222
00:15:43,760 --> 00:15:45,360
Domain Madagascar!

223
00:15:53,020 --> 00:15:54,660
A runic statue.

224
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:57,620
Ben-Dempleur, commis-je-la.

225
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,980
How long are you going to insist
on protecting this withered,

226
00:16:15,140 --> 00:16:16,840
good-for-nothing-hold-city?

227
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:18,310
Indefinitely.

228
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:24,320
Why must you disrespect what our
ancestors had held so sacred?

229
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:29,200
The past has nothing to do
with me, so why should I care?

230
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:30,757
That doesn't surprise me.

231
00:16:30,840 --> 00:16:32,781
Only the foolish say such things.

232
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:37,340
How dare you insult someone so powerful!

233
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,480
Super Punch Mountain!

234
00:16:40,980 --> 00:16:43,157
I've got to get away
from these ruins before

235
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:45,828
this simpleton destroys
what's left of them!

236
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:58,677
I chose to travel with Luffy.

237
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:02,017
But these ruins could hold
the clues to an unspoken

238
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,688
history that's been
lost to the world below?

239
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,940
How long do you plan on running?

240
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:56,260
I don't understand it.

241
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:58,600
You finally decided to face me?

242
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:00,117
Yes.

243
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,940
It's too late for you.

244
00:18:02,980 --> 00:18:03,980
Too late?

245
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:07,981
Even if you choose to
repent, I won't forgive you.

246
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:12,200
Oh, you won't forgive me, I see.

247
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:15,317
All because of these
shabby old ruins you adore.

248
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:18,282
A pile of rubble that
doesn't even belong to you.

249
00:18:19,340 --> 00:18:20,240
That's right.

250
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:22,820
Those ruins don't belong to anyone.

251
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:26,880
I've grown tired of this, and
I'm tired of talking to you.

252
00:18:27,080 --> 00:18:28,620
Well, not to worry.

253
00:18:28,760 --> 00:18:31,097
In just a few short
moments you won't have to

254
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:33,768
talk to me ever again
because unfortunately,

255
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:36,297
you're going to be crushed
to death underneath me!

256
00:18:36,380 --> 00:18:37,340
Rock Mountain!

257
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:42,860
I can unleash all of my
power on you in this place!

258
00:18:46,560 --> 00:18:49,980
All you do is charge
around like a clumsy bull!

259
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:54,541
With no regard for the weight of
the history that you've destroyed!

260
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:56,090
Hang!

261
00:19:00,800 --> 00:19:02,480
This body's too heavy.

262
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:19,820
I'll jump you to ribbons!

263
00:19:21,420 --> 00:19:23,020
That's Hadex Mountain!

264
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,120
My eyes!

265
00:19:26,260 --> 00:19:27,120
I can't see!

266
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:32,497
What are you doing?

267
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:34,457
Why did you turn the
dials around backwards?

268
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:35,952
You're going to kill me!

269
00:19:56,880 --> 00:20:00,409
What you have carelessly destroyed
were priceless treasures,

270
00:20:00,740 --> 00:20:02,857
relics so rare it would
be next to impossible?

271
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:04,705
to measure their actual worth.

272
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:09,932
It's true that history may repeat
itself, but people can't go back in time.

273
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:13,562
A stupid brute like you
wouldn't understand that.

274
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:16,600
I understand.

275
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:19,880
Please, please, I'm sorry.

276
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:22,200
Won't you forgive me?

277
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:24,088
That's out of the question.

278
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:31,214
Well, in that case, I'll have
to kill you, then won't I?

279
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:38,540
Ahh! My fingers! My fingers!

280
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:40,900
Snow blue!

281
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:45,610
Delphinium!

282
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:48,780
No! No!

283
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,350
No! No!

284
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:59,880
I'm afraid it's far too late for that.

285
00:21:09,620 --> 00:21:10,900
Clutch!

286
00:21:22,500 --> 00:21:25,080
That was certainly unpleasant.

287
00:21:39,700 --> 00:21:41,935
This should be the center of the city.

288
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:45,651
But it doesn't match up at all
with the map on the monitor.

289
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:50,551
The monitor of the entire city was
broken up and it was thrust into the sky.

290
00:22:59,560 --> 00:23:01,040
It's so strange.

291
00:23:01,620 --> 00:23:03,920
Could this really be the City of Gold?

292
00:23:05,520 --> 00:23:08,873
The size and the topography
are all completely different.

293
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:19,297
And what's most unnatural of all...

294
00:23:19,380 --> 00:23:21,640
The only entrance is at the top.

295
00:23:28,520 --> 00:23:29,350
Could it be?

296
00:23:58,020 --> 00:23:59,620
I think I can go below.

297
00:24:14,440 --> 00:24:15,760
It's so vast.

298
00:24:16,100 --> 00:24:18,159
The ruins really do go much deeper.

299
00:24:19,420 --> 00:24:24,361
I thought it was bizarre that all these
blue sea ruins had island clouds for ground.

300
00:24:25,860 --> 00:24:29,117
The ruins above are nothing more
than the upper parts of the city,

301
00:24:29,200 --> 00:24:30,729
eaten up by island clouds.

302
00:24:31,080 --> 00:24:32,551
There's still more below.

303
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,760
Light! Light!

304
00:25:33,960 --> 00:25:35,340
It's all so incredible.

305
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:38,620
The ancient city collapsed 800 years ago,

306
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:41,097
but I can hardly believe
it's been that long.

307
00:25:41,180 --> 00:25:43,420
It's still so majestic and grand.

308
00:25:43,700 --> 00:25:45,180
I've actually found it.

309
00:25:46,260 --> 00:25:49,620
This really is the great
Shandora, a city of gold.

310
00:26:13,320 --> 00:26:14,640
It can't be!

311
00:26:23,740 --> 00:26:24,580
So then,

312
00:26:24,780 --> 00:26:29,368
you're saying that it's possible our
lost history could actually be uncovered?

313
00:26:29,800 --> 00:26:33,212
And the Poneglyphs are the key
to unlocking these records?

314
00:26:42,280 --> 00:26:47,120
The ancient Poneglyph symbols, so the
Shendorians were familiar with them.

315
00:26:48,700 --> 00:26:52,524
But only the ones who made the
Poneglyphs were able to read them.

316
00:26:54,620 --> 00:26:57,820
We shall know the true meaning
and utter it to no one.

317
00:26:58,020 --> 00:27:00,844
It's our legacy to be the
inheritors of history,

318
00:27:01,080 --> 00:27:04,400
with the sounding of the Grand Belfry.

319
00:27:06,560 --> 00:27:07,500
That's right.

320
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:12,300
I remember Nolan's old logbook
mentioning a giant gold bell being here.

321
00:27:12,540 --> 00:27:14,800
But if that's true, where could it be?

322
00:27:16,420 --> 00:27:19,773
All of the city's ancient
writings were burned in a fire.

323
00:27:22,280 --> 00:27:25,380
The entire history of
this place was eradicated.

324
00:27:31,720 --> 00:27:33,557
They'll all manage somehow, right?

325
00:27:33,640 --> 00:27:36,405
They've come through this
kind of stuff before.

326
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:43,440
Quit following me!

327
00:27:46,460 --> 00:27:48,260
Sure goes down a long way.

328
00:27:53,640 --> 00:27:55,980
A poneglyph was carried into the city.

329
00:27:56,380 --> 00:27:57,937
There's no question about it.

330
00:27:58,020 --> 00:27:59,860
The city faced great hostility.

331
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:05,247
Shandora, the mystical city of gold,
fought and fell to protect that poneglyph.

332
00:28:09,240 --> 00:28:13,840
And that means the Grand Belfry located
in the center of the Four Altars.

333
00:28:14,940 --> 00:28:17,646
It could contain the
text of the true history.

334
00:28:17,960 --> 00:28:21,340
It could be the real poneglyph.
